      <div class="case-content">
        <section id="abstract">
          <h2>Abstract</h2>
          <p>
            Local agentic coding workflows increasingly span heterogeneous CLI agents—each backed by distinct model families, billing structures, and rolling subscription quotas (e.g., 5-hour and 7-day rate-limit windows). Running these tools independently forces developers to manually switch terminals, loses cross-session context, wastes substantial context tokens on raw file reads and verbose CLI output, and lacks deterministic safeguards against tool-call loops.
          </p>
          <p>
            We present <strong>Cockpit v2.2 (<code>agent-orchestrator</code>)</strong>, a native Rust + GPUI desktop orchestrator and concurrent stdio Model Context Protocol (MCP) server unifying Claude Code, Codex CLI, Antigravity, and OpenCode. In v2.2, the workspace spans <strong>73 Rust files (~78,000 LOC)</strong> across <strong>57 runtime modules</strong>, paired with a native <strong>Kotlin Android app (~2.7k LOC)</strong> and <strong>Python 3D/Observatory pipelines (~3.6k LOC)</strong>, verified by <strong>228 passing Rust unit tests</strong> (automatic RTK shims, delta telemetry, hot Auto-Failover, and $0 pipelines detailed in <a href="/en/lab/cockpit-rtk-telemetry-pipelines/">Paper 10</a>). Across our deterministic v1.0 ablation suite run directly on Cockpit's Rust codebase, structural skeletons cut tokens by <strong>94.13%</strong> on average (up to <strong>97.07%</strong> on <code>app.rs</code> in 38.0 ms), CLI filtering cuts verbose logs by <strong>84.94%</strong> (<strong>96.83%</strong> on 123-test <code>cargo test</code> output; <strong>−85.0%</strong> live via <code>cli_shims</code>), context compaction reduces an 18-turn session by <strong>88.34%</strong> (Capsule) and <strong>97.31%</strong> (5-line handoff), observation masking cuts stale tool output by <strong>69.51%</strong>, <code>LoopGuard</code> catches <strong>3/3</strong> loops with <strong>0 false positives</strong>, and deterministic routing achieves <strong>100.0%</strong> accuracy in <code>&lt; 20 µs</code>. Section 6 documents the implemented v2.x runtime subsystems separately from the v1.0 measured tables.
          </p>
        </section>

        <section id="intro-related">
          <h2>1. Introduction &amp; 2. Related Work</h2>
          <p>
            Operating heterogeneous CLIs concurrently exposes four systemic bottlenecks that model scaling alone does not solve: context bloat from raw reads and logs, search-and-replace edit fragility, silent tool-call loops, and fragmented 5h/7d quota visibility across providers. Cockpit addresses these bottlenecks at the local systems layer, building on empirical findings from:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Structural Localization:</strong> <em>AutoCodeRover</em> (<code>arXiv:2404.05427</code>), <em>Agentless</em> (<code>arXiv:2407.01489</code>), <em>RepoGraph</em> (<code>arXiv:2410.14684</code>), and <em>LocAgent</em> (<code>arXiv:2503.09089</code>) — operationalized in pure Rust (<code>fs_skeleton</code>, symbol-annotated <code>fs_search</code>, <code>blast_radius</code>) with sub-40 ms latency and zero external indexer daemon.</li>
            <li><strong>Diff Interfaces &amp; External Oracles:</strong> <em>Diff-XYZ</em> (<code>arXiv:2510.12487</code>), Huang et al. (<code>arXiv:2310.01798</code>), and <em>TDD-Bench Verified</em> (<code>arXiv:2412.02883</code>) — applied via hash-anchored reads (<code>hashline</code>), inline compiler verification (<code>fs_patch(..., verify: true)</code>), and pre-merge Git worktree quality gates.</li>
            <li><strong>Quota-Aware Routing &amp; Multi-Agent Scaling Limits:</strong> <em>RouteLLM</em> (<code>arXiv:2406.18665</code>), <em>MasRouter</em> (<code>arXiv:2502.11133</code>), <em>Puppeteer</em> (<code>arXiv:2505.19591</code>), <em>MAST</em> (<code>arXiv:2503.13657</code>), and <em>Towards a Science of Scaling Agent Systems</em> (<code>arXiv:2512.08296</code>) — motivating single-agent defaults, bounded delegation depth (<code>COCKPIT_DELEGATE_DEPTH=1</code>), and live quota-weighted routing.</li>
          </ul>
        </section>

        <section id="architecture">
          <h2>3. System Architecture</h2>
          <div class="arch-stack" role="img" aria-label="Three-layer Cockpit v2.0 Rust workspace architecture: orchestrator-ui, orchestrator-runtime, and orchestrator-core">
            <div class="arch-layer">
